cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jashwanth
    family-names: Mummalaneni
    affiliation: IIT Guwahati 2024
title: "Hawkes Process Calibration of Cryptocurrency Limit Order Book Data"
abstract: >
  A bivariate Sum-of-Exponentials Hawkes model is calibrated on BUY/SELL
  market order arrivals from Binance BTC/USDT and ETH/USDT limit order book
  data (144 to 145 rolling one-hour windows, May 2026). Mann-Whitney tests
  reject time-homogeneity at UTC 13:30 (NYSE regular open) on both assets
  (p < 0.005), and an OLS regression of the branching ratio η on UTC-hour
  dummies explains 35 to 39% of cross-window variance (R² = 0.352, bootstrap
  p = 0.001). η correlates with hourly realized volatility at Spearman
  ρ = 0.84. The time-rescaling Kolmogorov-Smirnov test fails on raw aggTrade
  streams (KS ≈ 0.50 to 0.62) and recovers after collapsing sub-100µs sweep
  fills into single events (KS ≈ 0.02 to 0.04), mirroring the order-ID-based
  filtration in Anantha, Jain and Maiti (2025).
version: "1.0.0"
